Theorem RL-32: all non-scalar parameters initialize Borrowed; fixpoint promotes to Owned

  Preconditions:
    - RL-32 governs borrow-inference initialization per Annex E §AIMS
      Borrow Inference: "All non-scalar parameters initialize Borrowed. The
      fixpoint promotes to Owned based on demand."
    - Signature ArcFunction x AimsStateMap -> ArcFunction per
      the canonical proof notation:264; discharged against the sec-01
      Realization.proof sorry obligation.
    - This is the IC-2 most-optimistic initialization (Access = Borrowed)
      promoted monotonically by IC-3 join toward Owned.
    - Shipped: borrow/mod.rs (borrow inference — Owned/Borrowed ABI decisions).
    - depends-on sec-06: IC-2 (param init) + IC-3 (param join).

  Soundness property:
    Forall non-scalar parameter p:

      (P1) Inference: p initializes Borrowed (the most optimistic ABI — the
           caller manages the reference); the monotone fixpoint promotes p to
           Owned iff demand proves the callee consumes / stores the value.

      (P2) Soundness (monotone toward conservative): Borrowed is the optimistic
           floor; promotion only INCREASES the ABI obligation (Borrowed <
           Owned per §AIMS §3.1), never decreases it, so the fixpoint converges
           and the final ABI never under-claims ownership the callee needs.

    RL-32 refines plain ARC's everything-Owned ABI by inferring Borrowed where
    the callee provably does not consume the value, eliminating the
    caller-inc / callee-dec pair at the boundary.

  Proof obligation:
    Constructive discharge by the case_analysis engine.

    Part (P1/P2) — inference grid:
      nonscalar_borrowed_init -> Borrowed (not consumed)
      nonscalar_consumed_owned -> Owned (consumed; promoted)
      scalar_borrowed -> Borrowed (no RC; never promoted)
      Coverage gate: 3 inference cases.

    Engines dispatched:
      case_analysis (PRIMARY —
        section_08::verify_rl32_borrowed_init_owned_promotion; inference grid;
        emits Fail on a wrong ABI inference)
      rc_counting (SECONDARY — gracious-accept per the coverage-manifest RL
        row)
      refinement (SECONDARY — gracious-accept per the coverage-manifest RL
        row)

  Expected:
    status: valid
    reason: section_08 case_analysis engine discharges RL-32 via the borrow-inference grid (non-scalar params init Borrowed; demand-driven promotion to Owned when consumed; scalars stay Borrowed/no-RC) as a monotone-toward-conservative fixpoint, grounded in the IC-2/IC-3 contracts + borrow/mod.rs
